Subject: Use uint8 for the similarity bitmap pointers

PostgreSQL 19 removes the bits8 alias. uint8 is available on every supported major and has the same width.

--- a/hamming.c
+++ b/hamming.c
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@
 {
 	VarBit		*a, *b;
 	int		alen, blen;
-	bits8		*pa, *pb;
+	uint8		*pa, *pb;
 	int		maxlen;
 	float8		res = 0.0;
 	int		i;
